<p>Use the following procedure to have several document pages arranged 
 on each print. This function is called Layout.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>When using Layout, a suitable reduction or enlargement 
 ratio is selected automatically based upon the paper size and the number 
 of sheets you want to fit on each page. For example, an A4 document would 
 be reduced in order to fit 2 pages on each sheet of A4 paper. An A5 document 
 would be printed with four A5 document pages fitted on each sheet of A3 
 paper.</p></li>
<li><p>If the page orientation varies within a document, 
 a page break will occur before a page where the orientation changes.</p></li>
<li><p>If an equivalent function is available from your 
 application, turn it off and use the printer driver function.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used 
 Settings</span> tab or the <span class="Term-Soft">2 Sided/Layout/Booklet</span> 
 menu of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select a layout type in the <span class="Term-Soft">Layout:</span> 
 list.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Click the <span class="Term-Soft">&lt;&lt; Collapse list</span> button if the <span class="Term-Soft">Layout:</span> 
 list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> tab 
 is not displayed.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="4">
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Page Order:</span> 
 list, select the page order.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Draw Border</span> 
 check box on the <span class="Term-Soft">2 Sided/Layout/Booklet</span> menu 
 of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab if you want 
 to print dotted separator lines for combined pages.</p></li>
<li><p>When specifying the orientation of an original 
 containing a mixture of landscape and portrait pages, click the <span class="Term-Soft">Mixed 
 Original Orientations...</span> button on the <span class="Term-Soft">2 
 Sided/Layout/Booklet</span> menu of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed 
 Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Select <span class="Term-Soft">Printer Defaults</span> for <span class="Term-Soft">Rotate 
 Mixed Original Orientation</span> on the <span class="Term-Soft">Output 
 Settings</span> menu in advance.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="7">
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
